---
layout: base
title: Blog
description: 'All blog posts can be found here'
pagination:
  data: collections.allPosts
  size: 8
permalink: 'blog/{% if pagination.pageNumber >=1 %}page-{{ pagination.pageNumber + 1 }}/{% endif %}index.html'
---

<div class="wrapper">
  {#- Was a `spot-color-theme-secondary` band: #eaeaea text on the #9a9a9a
     grey surface, about 1.9:1 -- well under the 4.5:1 minimum, and the
     accessibility pass is a stated Phase 1 requirement. Now matches the
     Services/Contact header pattern on the normal near-black surface. #}
  <header class="region flow" style="--region-space-top: var(--space-xl-2xl); --region-space-bottom: var(--space-s)">
    <h1 class="font-display">{{ title }}</h1>
  </header>

  {#- The starter printed its own pagination settings here as demo copy.
     Replaced with a real standing description of what the blog is, plus the
     feed link -- journalists and competition peers are an explicit audience
     (spec S3) and RSS is how they track a team without checking manually. #}
  <div class="region flow prose" style="--region-space-top: var(--space-l-xl); --region-space-bottom: var(--space-m)">
    <p>
      Build logs, competition writeups, and CTF notes — what we tried, what broke, and what we'd do differently.
    </p>
    <p class="text-step-min-1">
      <a class="button" data-small-button href="/feed.xml">Subscribe via RSS</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <custom-masonry layout="50-50">
		{% asyncEach item in pagination.items %}
			{% include "partials/card-blog.njk" %}
		{% endeach %}
	</custom-masonry>

  <!-- set collection to paginate -->
  {% set collectionToPaginate = collections.posts %}
  <!-- set target pagination settings in meta.js -->
  {% set metaKey = "blog" %}
  <!-- if the number of items in the collection is greater than the number of items shown on one page -->
  {% if collectionToPaginate.length > pagination.size %}
    <!-- include pagination -->
    {% include 'partials/pagination.njk' %}
  {% endif %}
</div>
